course: dictionary
lesson: 6131
title: Migrant
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A migrant is a person who moves from one place or country to another, often to find work or a better life. Look at the clues in this sentence: «A refugee is someone who fled war or danger to their life; a migrant moves to another country, often for work or a better life.» The words often, work and better life tell you why people move.
explain: The sentence also gives a contrast. A refugee flees danger, while a migrant moves for work or a better life. Both words are about moving, but the reason is different. Ask yourself: why did this person move?
explain: Migrant can also mean an animal, often a bird, that travels to a different place at certain seasons. Swallows are migrant birds: they fly south for the winter. The clues around the word tell you which meaning is being used.
fact: A migrant is a person who moves to another country, often for work or a better life.
fact: A migrant can also be an animal, often a bird, that travels to a different place at certain seasons.
fact: Migrant workers are people who move to another place to find work.
fact: Migration is the word for the moving itself.
fact: A refugee flees war or danger; a migrant moves mainly to find work or a better life.
exercise: «A migrant moves to another country, often for work or a better life.» What is a migrant? | A bird that cannot fly | *A person who moves to another country for work or a better life | A person who never leaves home
exercise: Science class says swallows are migrant birds. What does migrant mean here? | A bird kept in a cage | A bird that sings loudly all day | *A bird that travels to a different place at certain seasons | A bird that cannot fly
exercise: Which person is a migrant, not a refugee? | A family who fled a war | *A woman who moved abroad to find a better job | A child who ran from danger
test: In geography we study why people move. What is the name for the moving itself? | Migrant | Refugee | *Migration
test: «A migrant moves to another country, often for work or a better life.» Which reason is given for moving? | Fleeing a war | Going on holiday for a week | *Work or a better life | Playing in a sports team
exam: Which sentence uses migrant to mean an animal? | *The swallows are migrant birds that fly south in winter | A migrant family moved to Glasgow | The migrant workers picked the fruit | Dad is a migrant from Poland
